{"id": "EUVD-2026-72021", "enisaUuid": "230e417a-5108-3468-84d0-beccf641073a", "description": "The rpcap client code that processes a RPCAP_MSG_PACKET message received from the server incorrectly validates its headers.  A malicious server can send a crafted message and cause the client to treat up to 20 bytes of the client process memory beyond the end of the buffer as if it was a part of the captured packet.", "datePublished": "2026-09-05T18:51:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T15:17:19", "baseScore": 5.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://github.com/the-tcpdump-group/libpcap/commit/b9590d482986d64673712460aae1d48d11fa0473"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-18238", "GHSA-2xr5-28gv-34j3"], "assigner": "Tcpdump", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06bb1e28-f589-38fb-b71a-6ad75e11a19c", "product": {"name": "libpcap", "vendor": {"name": "The Tcpdump Group"}}, "product_version": "1.10.x <1.10.7"}, {"id": "54ceba07-4d7d-3d10-9c91-d577251b539c", "product": {"name": "libpcap", "vendor": {"name": "The Tcpdump Group"}}, "product_version": "1.9.x"}, {"id": "8388c9f3-efd5-3833-8627-be1620f186d4", "product": {"name": "libpcap", "vendor": {"name": "The Tcpdump Group"}}, "product_version": "1.8.x"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3fd4dc0b-dff4-32b8-b0ba-7f20d97e51de", "vendor": {"name": "The Tcpdump Group"}}], "isExploited": false}